# Object-Tab Columns after relationshipName (client "Format" layout)

These columns appear on every object-definition tab to the right of
`relationshipName` (column X), per the client's finalized **Format** sheet. Honor
them in all field work. **Locate each column by its HEADER NAME** (the client
keeps the order stable but header-driven lookup is mandatory and reshuffle-proof);
the 0-based indices below are only a fallback.

| Col | idx | Header | Meaning / handling |
|-----|----:|--------|--------------------|
| Y  | 24 | deleteConstraint | **Field-definition column.** Lookup delete behavior `SetNull`/`Restrict`/`Cascade`; blank = generator default. |
| Z  | 25 | Tab              | **Page-layout tab** placement (top-level tab on the record page). Consumed by `gen_tabbed_page.py`. |
| AA | 26 | section          | **Page-layout section** within a tab. Consumed by the page generators. |
| AB | 27 | SAPItemName      | Discussion column. **Ignore.** |
| AC | 28 | sourceItemNo     | Discussion column. **Ignore.** |
| AD | 29 | **IsDelete**     | **DELETE flag.** `TRUE`/`true` ⇒ the field must be **DELETED** from the org (destructive). Route to a separate DELETE set — never create/update it. Blank/`FALSE` = normal. |
| AE | 30 | **WIP**          | **Skip flag.** `TRUE`/`true`/`X`/`x` (any case) ⇒ the row is work-in-progress → **IGNORE entirely** (do not name, generate, deploy, or delete it). |
| AF | 31 | ConfirmComments  | Discussion column. **Ignore.** |
| AG | 32 | reviewComments   | Discussion column. **Ignore.** |
| AH | 33 | **GDC AI Tool Comments** | **AI review-comment column (OUR designated use).** The AI writes its review/validation/fix notes here — see below. (Formerly `FreeColumnGDC1`; header renamed by client request.) |
| AI | 34 | **Deployment Status** | **Per-field org deploy-status column (OUR designated use).** The AI writes whether the field is present in the target org — see below. (Formerly `FreeColumnGDC2`.) |
| AJ | 35 | FreeColumnGDC3 | Spare AI column — unassigned. |
| AK | 36 | **Field Label (EN)** | **English label** for Translation Workbench (`CustomObjectTranslation` `en_US`). Header aliases: `Field Label (EN)`, `項目ラベル名 (EN)`. Formerly spare `FreeColumnGDC4`. Tabs without this header are untranslated. See `sf-object-translation-deploy.mdc`. |
| AL–BA | 37–52 | FreeColumnGDC5–20 | Spare AI columns — unassigned; available for future AI purposes. |
| BB–BV | 53–73 | actor / Persona cols | Actor columns for field-level security **later**. **Ignore for now.** |
| BW+ | 74+ | FreeColumnJP1…  | Discussion columns. **Ignore.** |

## Rules

1. **WIP skip (AE):** skip any row whose `WIP` column = `TRUE`/`true`/`X`/`x`
   (case-insensitive). Treat it as not present — never name, generate, deploy, or
   delete it.
2. **IsDelete (AD):** a row with `IsDelete` = `TRUE`/`true` is a **deletion**
   request → put it in a separate DELETE set handled by the destructive-deploy
   flow (see `sf-deploy-delta-and-blockers.mdc`). It is NOT a create/update and
   must never be part of the normal field package. A row that is BOTH WIP and
   IsDelete is skipped (WIP wins).
3. **Live reads:** never evaluate WIP or IsDelete from a cached snapshot — read
   the sheet live (`read-sheet-live.mdc`).
4. **Header-driven columns:** locate `Tab`, `section`, `IsDelete`, `WIP`,
   `GDC AI Tool Comments` (AH), `Deployment Status` (AI), `fullName`, and
   `Field Label (EN)` by header name (fall back to the indices above only
   if the header is absent). The scripts `fetch_sheet.py`, `mark_wip.py`,
   `write_back.py`, `write_ai_comments.py`, `write_deploy_status.py`,
   `plan_deploy.py` follow this. Note AH's header text is now
   **`GDC AI Tool Comments`** (was `FreeColumnGDC1`) — match either for
   backwards-compat, prefer the new name.
5. **Tab (Z) + section (AA):** page-layout inputs — `Tab` = top-level record-page
   tab, `section` = section within it. Consume only when doing page-layout work.
6. **Discussion columns (AB, AC, AF, AG, BW+):** never write to them; they belong
   to the user's discussion.
7. **Actor columns (BB–BV):** reserved for field-level security later — do not
   read or write them until the user asks.
8. **Column Y (deleteConstraint):** field-definition column; read for Lookup
   delete behavior, leave blank unless the user specifies a value.
9. **Block-end markers `END[…]` (Column A):** each block on a tab is terminated by
   an `END[XXX]` cell in **Column A**, where `XXX` names the block — i.e.
   `END[XXX]` marks the end of the area corresponding to `XXX` (confirmed by the
   sheet owner Takeaki Yagai, 2026-09-01). See the section below; the **field
   list ends at `END[項目]`** and nothing past it is a field.

## Block markers — `END[…]` (field-list / area boundaries)

Every "Format"-style object tab is split into stacked blocks, each closed by an
`END[XXX]` cell in **Column A** (the `No.` column, which otherwise only holds row
numbers). `END[XXX]` = end of the area whose header is `XXX`. Observed order:

| Marker (Col A) | Closes block | 
|-----|-----|
| **`END[項目]`** | **the FIELD list** (this is the field-scan terminator) |
| `END[レコードタイプ]` | Record Types |
| `END[入力規則]` | Validation Rules |
| `END[ルックアップ検索条件]` | Lookup Search Filters |

Rules:
- The FIELD list is always the FIRST block, so the **first `END[...]` cell
  (`END[項目]`) is the authoritative end-of-field-list marker.** STOP the field
  scan there — never parse Record-Type / Validation-Rule / Lookup-Filter rows as
  fields (doing so produces bogus "missing label/type/API name" validation
  errors).
- `fetch_sheet.py` enforces this: it breaks the row scan on the first Column-A
  cell starting with `END[` (`FIELD_LIST_END_PREFIX`). The older gray-guard line
  (`行挿入する場合は当行より上部`, col C) is kept only as a fallback for legacy tabs
  that predate the `END[…]` convention.
- These markers are read LIVE with the rest of the tab (`read-sheet-live.mdc`);
  never infer the boundary from a cached snapshot.

## AI review-comment column — AH (`GDC AI Tool Comments`)

The AI records its review comments in **AH** (header **`GDC AI Tool Comments`**,
formerly `FreeColumnGDC1`) on the specific field row they concern, at two stages:
- **Stage 1 — sheet validation:** each `validate_sheet.py` ERROR/WARN becomes a
  `[VALIDATION <date>] <check>: <message>` note on that field's AH cell.
- **Stage 2 — on-the-go deploy fix:** any fix the AI applies during deploy becomes
  a `[FIX <date>] <note>` on that field's AH cell.

Use `scripts/write_ai_comments.py` (`--report` for stage 1, `--fixes` for stage 2).
It APPENDS to existing AH text (never clobbers), de-dupes identical lines, and
skips WIP rows. Writing AH is a **gated sheet write** (`sheet-write-confirmation.mdc`):
preview the `cell: old → new` diff and get the user's confirmation before `--apply`.

## Deployment-status column — AI (`Deployment Status`)

Column **AI** (header **`Deployment Status`**, formerly `FreeColumnGDC2`) records,
per field row, whether that field is actually present in the target org, checked
LIVE against the object. Locate it by header name (fallback index 34).

Allowed values written by the tool:
- **`Deployed`** — the field's API name EXISTS in the target org (custom field
  confirmed via the Tooling `CustomField` object — FLS-independent — or a known
  standard field).
- **`Not Deployed`** — a deployable custom field (`__c`) whose API name is NOT in
  the org.
- **`Standard`** — a standard field (no `__c`, e.g. `OwnerId`, `Name`,
  `CreatedDate`) — always present, not tool-deployed.
- **`Deleted`** — a field row processed as a DELETION (IsDelete=TRUE) that was
  actually removed from the org (confirmed live absent via the Tooling
  `CustomField` object after the destructive deploy). Set this on every deleted
  row so the sheet reflects the destructive operation.
- (WIP rows are skipped; blank-API/noise rows are skipped.)

**AI must always mirror the LAST operation on the row** (see
`sf-deploy-status-column-always.mdc`): after a create/update deploy the row's AI
is `Deployed`; after a destructive delete the row's AI is `Deleted`. Updating AI
based on the operation is MANDATORY, not optional.

Rules:
- The status is always derived from a LIVE org check (Tooling API for custom
  fields — never `sobject describe`, which is FLS-gated), per object, at write
  time. Never infer it from a cached snapshot or a deploy log.
- Refresh AI after every deploy (see `sf-post-deploy-fls-and-flexipage.mdc`) and
  whenever the user asks for a field-level deploy-status snapshot.
- Writing AI is a **gated sheet write** (`sheet-write-confirmation.mdc`): preview
  the `cell: old → new` diff and get the user's confirmation before applying. The
  helper is `scripts/write_deploy_status.py`.

## Highlighting convention (MANDATORY)

When highlighting rows (blockers, formula fills, WIP, etc.), color **only the
Column A ("No.") cell** of the target row — never the whole row / data-column
span. Colleagues color cells in the data columns for their own review, so
whole-row fills would overwrite their work. The scripts `highlight_rows.py` and
`highlight_blockers.py` are fixed to Column A only (`START_COL, END_COL = 0, 1`);
keep it that way. Highlighting is still a gated sheet write.
